          <h2>How I work as a Web Developer in Cologne and Berlin</h2>
          <p>
            Cologne, Berlin, Rhein and Ruhr have some things in common: Openness, honesty, and diversity. Newcomers are integrated and become proud of their new home. Diverse culture influences and proximity to neighboring countries have always fostered exchange and inspiration in the major cities of NRW. From a business perspective, Cologne and NRW, like Berlin, host plenty of companies, agencies, startups and freelance service providers, who inspire one another and collaborate eventually.
          </p>
          <p>
            Train trips through mobile dead zones in the Bergisches Land hills keep reminding us not to code solely for ideal conditions. I am happy to offer honest, constructive criticism and propose my own solutions, if you wish. Thorough, productive, and swift.
          </p>
          <p>
            This already says a lot about how I work as a web developer. Important to me, especially in times of artificial intelligence and increasing automation, is to stay human, to listen, and to explain in an understandable way.
          </p>

          <h2>Communication and Documentation in Cologne/NRW or Online</h2>

